# Obsidian Vault Markdown Standards

Apply these rules when editing markdown in this vault.

## Document Structure
- Keep a clear H1 title and concise section headers.
- Include `## Related` with valid Obsidian backlinks for connected docs.
- Prefer operational sections: Purpose, Run, Risks, Incident, Related.
- For project README files, include mandatory sections: `Project Location`, `Stack`, and link to `requirements.md`.
- For skill notes in `60_skills/`: `Purpose`, `Skill Location`, `Triggers`, `Related Projects`, `Related`.

## Skills Registry
- Local project skills only — not default Cursor/plugin skills.
- Path: `60_skills/<owner>/<skill-name>.md`; owner = project slug or `workspace` for cross-project.
- After creating `<SKILLS_ROOT>/<name>/SKILL.md`, register in Obsidian in the same turn (see [[50_runbooks/skills-for-cursor]]).

## Metadata and Traceability
- Preserve YAML frontmatter with closing `---`.
- Required fields on meaningful edits: `tags`, `last_verified`, `change_source`.
- Keep contextual `tags` up to date when document scope changes.
- Avoid orphan notes; link project docs to infra/db/runbook context.

## Linking Rules
- Always use path-qualified wikilinks: `[[10_projects/example_library/runbook]]`.
- Project `## Related` must include README + the other three core docs where applicable.
- Forbid self-links in `## Related`.
- Profile hub notes (`00_profile/*`) should link to all active `10_projects/*/README`.

## Stack Normalization
- Format: `Python: X.Y` → `DB: ...` → `Selenium: да/нет` → `Core libs: ...`
- Document your Python contour split if more than one interpreter is in use.

## Content Quality
- Keep instructions executable (real commands and paths *for your* machine; until filled, use `<VAULT>`, `<SKILLS_ROOT>`, `<PROJECT_ROOT>`, `<GIT_REMOTE>`).
- Remove stale or contradictory statements in the same edit.
- Prefer short, actionable bullets over long prose.
- Do not use placeholder citations like `[web:12]`.

## SCM Naming Policy
- Document your canonical remote as `<GIT_REMOTE>` in project README when a repo exists.
- This template publishes via GitHub. Some teams use self-hosted Forgejo or another host for operational remotes. Do not copy a publisher URL into operational notes.

